# Read by every MSBuild run started from this directory tree (dotnet build, test, publish).
# Reused worker nodes outlive the build that started them, and a concurrent build can't
# borrow a busy one, so parallel builds stack up one node per CPU thread each until the
# machine runs out of memory. With reuse off, workers exit with their build.
#
# A -maxcpucount cap can't live here: the dotnet CLI always passes a bare -maxcpucount,
# and command-line switches override this file.
-nodeReuse:false
